00:17:13,785 --> 00:17:15,065
They're practically
an endangered species anyway.

265
00:17:15,145 --> 00:17:16,224
Let's use them.

266
00:17:16,785 --> 00:17:18,145
I agree.

267
00:17:18,224 --> 00:17:19,224
Okay.

268
00:17:19,305 --> 00:17:21,464
-Tungtae!
-Tae!

269
00:17:21,545 --> 00:17:23,105
-Go ahead, little Bro.
-Tungtae!

270
00:17:23,184 --> 00:17:25,704
Come on, tell your boss the good news.

271
00:17:25,785 --> 00:17:26,825
What queue number did you get?

272
00:17:26,905 --> 00:17:28,065
Number one, Bro.

273
00:17:30,185 --> 00:17:32,465
-You're amazing.
-Number one hundred, Bro.

274
00:17:33,625 --> 00:17:35,425
-You little punk.
-Want to fight me?

275
00:17:35,505 --> 00:17:37,545
One hundred?

276
00:17:38,065 --> 00:17:40,425
I sent you so early,
and you still got number 100?

277
00:17:40,505 --> 00:17:42,905
There were too many people. I did my best.

278
00:17:44,185 --> 00:17:45,265
Let's grab something to eat.

279
00:17:45,345 --> 00:17:47,385
-This line is insanely long.
-Yeah.

280
00:17:47,465 --> 00:17:48,745
Seriously, I'm getting hungry.

281
00:17:48,825 --> 00:17:49,865
Come on.

282
00:17:49,945 --> 00:17:52,505
-Don't blame the kid.
-I rushed here first thing.

283
00:17:53,745 --> 00:17:56,145
-Number 25.
-What?

284
00:17:56,225 --> 00:17:57,225
-Number 25.
-Only 25 so far?

285
00:17:57,305 --> 00:17:58,625
Only number 25?

286
00:18:12,825 --> 00:18:14,185
Who's that?

287
00:18:18,185 --> 00:18:20,265
Hey, that's Newyear.

288
00:18:20,345 --> 00:18:21,305
Newyear?

289
00:18:21,385 --> 00:18:23,425
-Newyear!
-Hey, Newyear!

290
00:18:23,945 --> 00:18:26,145
-Newyear!
-Newyear!

291
00:18:26,225 --> 00:18:28,905
Even Newyear came to Jia for a reading.

292
00:18:28,985 --> 00:18:30,585
-Newyear.
-Let's go.

293
00:18:31,985 --> 00:18:34,065
Number 100.

294
00:18:35,665 --> 00:18:36,945
This has to be the place.

295
00:18:37,025 --> 00:18:38,065
Go on, have a seat.

296
00:18:38,145 --> 00:18:40,225
-You're the one getting the reading.
-Sit down.

297
00:18:42,905 --> 00:18:44,065
Hang in there.

298
00:18:44,145 --> 00:18:45,745
Once you see the fortune teller,

299
00:18:45,825 --> 00:18:46,985
you'll feel better.

300
00:18:47,065 --> 00:18:49,145
-You'll be fine. Trust me.
-Yeah, trust him.

301
00:18:49,225 --> 00:18:50,505
But I don't know.

302
00:18:50,585 --> 00:18:53,665
The only one I want is Faye,
not a fortune teller.

303
00:18:56,825 --> 00:18:58,505
-Hey, wait.
-Hold on.

304
00:18:58,585 --> 00:19:00,585
-You haven't had your fortune read yet.
-Jia's here.

305
00:19:12,665 --> 00:19:15,145
Damn, he's a real fashion icon.

306
00:19:15,225 --> 00:19:16,425
Sit down.

307
00:19:16,505 --> 00:19:17,705
Why are you all standing over me?

308
00:19:19,545 --> 00:19:21,065
-You.
-Go on.

309
00:19:21,145 --> 00:19:22,225
You're getting your fortune read.

310
00:19:28,505 --> 00:19:29,705
Date of birth?

311
00:19:30,905 --> 00:19:31,945
Tell him.

312
00:19:32,025 --> 00:19:32,985
Why are you looking at me?

313
00:19:33,065 --> 00:19:36,065
March 7th, 2009.

314
00:19:50,145 --> 00:19:51,665
You were just in an accident, weren't you?

315
00:19:53,905 --> 00:19:55,105
What?

316
00:19:56,905 --> 00:19:58,265
A love accident?

317
00:19:58,345 --> 00:20:00,105
Something you never saw coming.

318
00:20:01,785 --> 00:20:04,425
You got hurt in the head and it cracked.

319
00:20:05,545 --> 00:20:06,905
Your "heart."

320
00:20:06,985 --> 00:20:08,225
That's what he meant.

321
00:20:09,745 --> 00:20:10,905
Is he really that accurate?

322
00:20:10,985 --> 00:20:12,145
He is.

323
00:20:12,225 --> 00:20:13,745
Exactly.

324
00:20:13,825 --> 00:20:14,825
Or maybe because his eyes are closed,

325
00:20:14,905 --> 00:20:16,545
he can't see our reactions

326
00:20:16,625 --> 00:20:18,025
to know he got everything wrong.

327
00:20:20,465 --> 00:20:21,385
Dream.

328
00:20:23,905 --> 00:20:25,345
You dream of becoming a pilot.

329
00:20:25,425 --> 00:20:26,385
That'll be difficult.

330
00:20:30,145 --> 00:20:31,825
-I…
-Hey.

331
00:20:31,905 --> 00:20:34,145
I've never wanted to be a pilot.

332
00:20:34,825 --> 00:20:37,345
I think he's just making things up.

333
00:20:37,425 --> 00:20:38,945
Indy's terrified of flying.

334
00:20:40,545 --> 00:20:42,585
I don't think fortune-telling is for me.

335
00:20:42,665 --> 00:20:44,545
-I'm leaving.
-Let's go.

336
00:20:44,625 --> 00:20:46,265
-He's totally making it up.
-Hey.

337
00:20:46,345 --> 00:20:48,345
Wait, wait.

338
00:20:48,425 --> 00:20:49,465
At least give him a chance.

339
00:20:50,545 --> 00:20:51,945
He might miss with cold readings,

340
00:20:52,025 --> 00:20:53,905
but tarot is his signature.

341
00:20:54,545 --> 00:20:55,785
Give him a chance.

342
00:20:55,865 --> 00:20:57,985
-What's with you?
-Let him draw the cards first.

343
00:20:58,065 --> 00:20:59,625
-Trust me.
-Fine, just this once.

344
00:20:59,705 --> 00:21:00,665
Trust me.

345
00:21:00,745 --> 00:21:02,905
You just got your heart broken
by someone older, didn't you?

346
00:21:06,305 --> 00:21:07,345
Shit.

347
00:21:07,425 --> 00:21:08,985
-Told you.
-Spot on.

348
00:21:09,065 --> 00:21:10,665
-Sit down.
-You.

349
00:21:10,745 --> 00:21:11,705
Yes.

350
00:21:18,505 --> 00:21:19,945
You were really hurt.

351
00:21:20,745 --> 00:21:21,905
The cards also say

352
00:21:21,985 --> 00:21:23,185
that person has a high profile,

353
00:21:23,265 --> 00:21:26,105
like an emperor. The best of the best.

354
00:21:28,985 --> 00:21:29,985
Spot on.

355
00:21:31,345 --> 00:21:33,225
See? I told you.

356
00:21:36,545 --> 00:21:38,425
Shuffle the cards
if you want to know more.

357
00:21:54,505 --> 00:21:55,665
Come on.

358
00:21:56,705 --> 00:21:58,105
Give one to him.

359
00:22:06,865 --> 00:22:09,425
The love you hoped for won't come true.

360
00:22:09,505 --> 00:22:11,665
But the love you're
not looking for is close by.

361
00:22:12,345 --> 00:22:13,585
Simply put,

362
00:22:14,185 --> 00:22:15,545
it's someone in your class.

363
00:22:17,625 --> 00:22:18,705
Who is it?

364
00:22:24,345 --> 00:22:25,585
Excuse me, fortune teller.

365
00:22:30,105 --> 00:22:31,305
What's he doing?

366
00:22:31,905 --> 00:22:32,905
No idea.

367
00:22:38,585 --> 00:22:39,905
I want to ask about my studies.

368
00:22:40,585 --> 00:22:42,185
Will I get into architecture school?

369
00:22:42,865 --> 00:22:44,225
These cards aren't about your studies.

370
00:22:44,905 --> 00:22:45,785
They're about love.

371
00:22:48,065 --> 00:22:50,145
Someone's about to confess to you.

372
00:22:53,185 --> 00:22:54,265
And if you date,

373
00:22:54,345 --> 00:22:57,065
it's going to be amazing.

374
00:22:57,145 --> 00:22:58,185
A total hit.

375
00:23:00,745 --> 00:23:02,905
Is it the one you have a crush on?

376
00:23:03,985 --> 00:23:05,225
Who is it, fortune teller?

377
00:23:06,465 --> 00:23:07,665
I can't tell you.

378
00:23:08,185 --> 00:23:09,345
That's all the cards reveal.

379
00:23:09,425 --> 00:23:10,825
When the time comes,

380
00:23:10,905 --> 00:23:11,945
the truth will reveal itself.

381
00:23:13,625 --> 00:23:15,105
<i>Why am I even getting worked up?</i>

382
00:23:20,545 --> 00:23:21,545
Actually, you can get another reading.

383
00:23:22,345 --> 00:23:23,945
One reading per person.

384
00:23:24,025 --> 00:23:25,105
JIA'S SHRINE

385
00:23:25,185 --> 00:23:27,145
Damn it, you're missing the point.

386
00:23:27,225 --> 00:23:28,545
We're here for Indy's reading.

387
00:23:29,225 --> 00:23:30,385
Come on, let's step outside.

388
00:23:30,465 --> 00:23:31,945
Give them some privacy.

389
00:23:32,785 --> 00:23:34,505
So they can talk in peace.

390
00:23:35,265 --> 00:23:36,385
Come on, you've got this.

391
00:23:36,465 --> 00:23:37,705
Don't overthink it.

392
00:23:38,385 --> 00:23:39,945
Ask him whatever you want.

393
00:23:40,025 --> 00:23:40,985
Go, go, go.

394
00:23:41,065 --> 00:23:42,225
You too.

395
00:23:42,305 --> 00:23:43,425
Take your bag.

396
00:23:48,265 --> 00:23:50,185
Now it's your turn.

397
00:23:53,265 --> 00:23:54,545
I…

398
00:23:54,625 --> 00:23:56,185
want to move on.

399
00:23:56,265 --> 00:23:57,385
How do I do that?

400
00:24:13,945 --> 00:24:16,385
The cards say
you need to try something new.

401
00:24:16,465 --> 00:24:17,745
That's hard.

402
00:24:17,825 --> 00:24:20,945
Everything I do reminds me of her.

403
00:24:25,265 --> 00:24:28,265
Actually, joining the initiation ritual
will definitely help.

404
00:24:30,505 --> 00:24:32,025
If you're interested, message me.

405
00:24:34,265 --> 00:24:35,665
JIRAKORN RERKSAKONRAT

406
00:24:36,985 --> 00:24:38,705
I am. I'm interested.

407
00:24:39,825 --> 00:24:41,825
Then the first Saturday after finals.

408
00:24:42,505 --> 00:24:45,985
-Okay.
-At exactly 12:25 p.m.

409
00:24:46,065 --> 00:24:47,025
I'll send you the location.

410
00:24:47,985 --> 00:24:51,425
For the remaining 30 minutes,
ask me anything.

411
00:25:02,265 --> 00:25:03,785
You're very hardworking.

412
00:25:03,865 --> 00:25:05,745
You don't need the cards. You'll get in.

413
00:25:07,625 --> 00:25:09,625
You never know.

414
00:25:09,705 --> 00:25:11,145
There could be lots of people
who work harder than me.

415
00:25:15,185 --> 00:25:16,105
Oh, right.

416
00:25:16,185 --> 00:25:17,825
About what the fortune teller said…

417
00:25:18,425 --> 00:25:20,705
That someone would confess to you.

418
00:25:20,785 --> 00:25:21,945
Anyone come to mind?

419
00:25:23,425 --> 00:25:25,025
You seem more curious than I am.

420
00:25:27,265 --> 00:25:29,065
Maybe I'm just being nosy.

421
00:25:39,745 --> 00:25:41,665
Damn, that's awesome.

422
00:25:41,745 --> 00:25:42,705
What's this called again?

423
00:25:42,785 --> 00:25:44,265
This one?

424
00:25:44,345 --> 00:25:46,145
It's called line practice.

425
00:25:47,145 --> 00:25:48,585
It's for controlling pressure.

426
00:25:49,105 --> 00:25:50,425
And training hand-eye coordination.

427
00:25:53,945 --> 00:25:55,105
How long have you been practicing?

428
00:25:57,385 --> 00:25:59,465
-About three years, I guess.
-Damn.

429
00:25:59,545 --> 00:26:01,425
That's as long as
I've been playing guitar.

430
00:26:01,505 --> 00:26:02,785
But damn,

431
00:26:02,865 --> 00:26:04,385
I still can't hit the right chords.

432
00:26:05,065 --> 00:26:07,545
I've thrown away plenty of sketches too.

433
00:26:09,825 --> 00:26:11,225
Can I see?

434
00:26:16,785 --> 00:26:17,825
No.

435
00:26:24,385 --> 00:26:25,225
It's beautiful.

436
00:26:30,145 --> 00:26:30,985
Wait.

437
00:26:31,585 --> 00:26:32,865
Can you draw me?

438
00:26:32,945 --> 00:26:35,145
No. Drawing people is hard.

439
00:26:35,225 --> 00:26:36,585
There are too many details.

440
00:26:38,345 --> 00:26:40,345
It can't be harder
than the buildings you draw.

441
00:26:40,425 --> 00:26:42,145
Whatever these are.
What's with all these pillars?

442
00:26:44,305 --> 00:26:45,625
Please.

443
00:26:45,705 --> 00:26:47,425
You won't know until you try. Please.

444
00:26:47,505 --> 00:26:49,105
People show their emotions.

445
00:26:50,265 --> 00:26:51,425
I'm still a beginner.

446
00:26:51,505 --> 00:26:52,785
Please.

447
00:26:53,305 --> 00:26:54,625
Will you draw me?

448
00:26:56,985 --> 00:26:57,945
So you will?

449
00:26:58,025 --> 00:26:59,705
Yeah, I'll draw you.

450
00:27:02,225 --> 00:27:04,745
So, how still do I have to sit?

451
00:27:06,585 --> 00:27:08,745
As still as you can.

452
00:27:09,745 --> 00:27:10,745
And,

453
00:27:11,665 --> 00:27:12,625
where should I look?

454
00:27:12,705 --> 00:27:13,825
Over there?

455
00:27:14,745 --> 00:27:15,585
You can look at me.

456
00:27:19,585 --> 00:27:20,705
Stay still.

457
00:27:35,185 --> 00:27:37,345
<i>Then date me.</i>

458
00:27:37,425 --> 00:27:38,585
<i>Shit.</i>

459
00:27:38,665 --> 00:27:39,785
<i>That voice is back.</i>

460
00:27:40,385 --> 00:27:41,585
Hey.

461
00:27:41,665 --> 00:27:43,385
You're fidgeting too much.

462
00:27:43,465 --> 00:27:44,625
Sit a little more still.

463
00:27:45,225 --> 00:27:46,505
Okay, okay.

464
00:27:48,065 --> 00:27:49,945
<i>Don't let that voice win.</i>

465
00:27:50,025 --> 00:27:51,625
<i>You made that rule yourself.</i>

466
00:27:51,705 --> 00:27:53,425
<i>And he already likes someone.</i>

467
00:27:53,505 --> 00:27:54,825
<i>Besides,</i>

468
00:27:54,905 --> 00:27:56,785
<i>it's someone really close to him.</i>

469
00:28:33,385 --> 00:28:34,465
Done.

470
00:28:39,625 --> 00:28:41,185
Whoa, that was fast.

471
00:28:41,265 --> 00:28:42,545
You're Picasso.

472
00:28:43,465 --> 00:28:45,305
See? I told you.

473
00:28:47,785 --> 00:28:48,905
Wait, wait.

474
00:28:49,585 --> 00:28:50,785
-Can I…
-What?

475
00:28:50,865 --> 00:28:52,065
Can I have the drawing?

476
00:28:52,145 --> 00:28:54,225
Please. I want it.

477
00:28:54,305 --> 00:28:56,225
Keep it and it'll give you nightmares.

478
00:28:57,705 --> 00:28:58,905
Probably.

479
00:29:00,785 --> 00:29:02,425
You could at least encourage me.

480
00:29:03,505 --> 00:29:04,585
Come on.

481
00:29:06,105 --> 00:29:07,785
Here, once you've done more drawings,

482
00:29:07,865 --> 00:29:10,265
I'm sure you'll get much better.

483
00:29:11,265 --> 00:29:12,105
Just keep drawing me.

484
00:29:12,185 --> 00:29:14,225
Draw my face over and over.

485
00:29:14,745 --> 00:29:16,785
When you make a better version,

486
00:29:16,865 --> 00:29:18,345
you can trade it for this one.

487
00:29:21,025 --> 00:29:21,945
Mm.

488
00:29:25,985 --> 00:29:27,185
Wait.

489
00:29:27,705 --> 00:29:28,825
Sign this for me.

490
00:29:29,465 --> 00:29:30,625
Right here.

491
00:29:32,345 --> 00:29:33,825
Why do I have to sign?

492
00:29:36,065 --> 00:29:37,185
Here.

493
00:29:37,265 --> 00:29:38,545
Why do I have to sign?

494
00:29:38,625 --> 00:29:40,665
The blood pact is sealed now.

495
00:29:41,425 --> 00:29:42,825
I'll wait until you're famous.

496
00:29:42,905 --> 00:29:44,225
Puttcasso.

497
00:29:45,905 --> 00:29:47,105
You're so lame.

498
00:29:53,785 --> 00:29:59,945
SEMESTER BREAK

499
00:30:11,705 --> 00:30:13,505
How am I supposed to know?

500
00:30:33,465 --> 00:30:35,305
How am I supposed to know?

501
00:30:42,105 --> 00:30:44,465
-Hello.
-Turn left.

502
00:30:49,185 --> 00:30:51,465
There's no way I'd miss you.

503
00:30:51,545 --> 00:30:53,265
You're basically a landmark.

504
00:31:00,385 --> 00:31:01,425
The timing is perfect.

505
00:31:01,505 --> 00:31:03,185
Where's the ritual, fortune teller?

506
00:31:03,265 --> 00:31:04,505
Right here.

507
00:31:05,585 --> 00:31:06,785
Ready?

508
00:31:07,305 --> 00:31:09,185
Ready to make a wish?

509
00:31:09,265 --> 00:31:11,545
May only good things come your way.

510
00:31:14,065 --> 00:31:15,065
Let's go.

511
00:31:16,385 --> 00:31:18,145
The first ritual starts here.

512
00:31:19,345 --> 00:31:21,225
In a barbershop, fortune teller?

513
00:31:22,105 --> 00:31:23,425
Just call me Jia.

514
00:31:23,505 --> 00:31:24,985
I meant to tell you that day.

515
00:31:25,065 --> 00:31:26,705
Call me whatever but that.

516
00:31:27,865 --> 00:31:29,185
Alright then.

517
00:31:30,265 --> 00:31:32,145
Hurry up. I booked your slot.

518
00:31:32,225 --> 00:31:33,825
If we're late, we'll lose it.

519
00:31:34,665 --> 00:31:35,985
The 12:25 slot.

520
00:31:36,065 --> 00:31:37,705
This is a haircut appointment?

521
00:31:38,265 --> 00:31:39,665
Don't question the fortune teller,

522
00:31:39,745 --> 00:31:41,225
or you'll jinx me.

523
00:31:49,825 --> 00:31:50,825
How is it?

524
00:31:51,905 --> 00:31:53,425
I feel like a new person.

525
00:31:55,305 --> 00:31:56,985
We're not done yet.

526
00:31:57,065 --> 00:31:59,385
-Really? What's next?
-Come on. Let's go.

527
00:32:02,025 --> 00:32:04,025
Damn, this feels so weird.

528
00:32:11,905 --> 00:32:13,585
You need something new.

529
00:32:14,585 --> 00:32:15,665
When you find something new,

530
00:32:15,745 --> 00:32:17,505
it's easier to let go of the past.

531
00:32:18,305 --> 00:32:19,505
Really, fortune teller?

532
00:32:22,225 --> 00:32:23,705
You can burn this outfit tomorrow.

533
00:32:24,465 --> 00:32:25,505
But for today,

534
00:32:27,945 --> 00:32:29,105
wear it, and pretend

535
00:32:31,465 --> 00:32:32,905
you're someone else.

536
00:32:42,905 --> 00:32:44,385
Something like that.

537
00:32:46,385 --> 00:32:47,665
Let's go.

538
00:32:47,745 --> 00:32:49,305
Go where?

539
00:32:49,385 --> 00:32:50,505
There's more?

540
00:32:51,025 --> 00:32:52,505
Get ready to sweat.

541
00:32:52,585 --> 00:32:53,905
You've cried enough already. Let's go.

542
00:33:45,465 --> 00:33:46,385
There you go.

543
00:33:50,665 --> 00:33:51,545
How do you feel?

544
00:33:55,865 --> 00:33:57,185
I feel great.

545
00:33:58,425 --> 00:34:01,105
You've released all that old energy.

546
00:34:02,865 --> 00:34:03,705
Next,

547
00:34:03,785 --> 00:34:06,425
delete every contact named Faye.

548
00:34:09,264 --> 00:34:10,744
Do I really have to go that far?

549
00:34:12,385 --> 00:34:13,385
According to the belief,

550
00:34:13,465 --> 00:34:16,145
change starts by letting go of the old.

551
00:34:16,225 --> 00:34:18,225
So there's room for something new.

552
00:34:18,304 --> 00:34:19,705
This is the final step.

553
00:34:21,945 --> 00:34:22,945
Your phone, please.

554
00:34:31,304 --> 00:34:32,744
It's like cleaning your house.

555
00:34:32,824 --> 00:34:34,264
If you don't throw old things away,

556
00:34:34,344 --> 00:34:36,264
there won't be room for anything new.

557
00:34:39,824 --> 00:34:44,385
FAYE.NAREEYA - FOLLOWING

558
00:34:47,385 --> 00:34:48,344
Fine.

559
00:34:48,425 --> 00:34:49,425
Let's do it.

560
00:34:50,665 --> 00:34:51,505
UNFOLLOW

561
00:34:51,585 --> 00:34:53,545
FOLLOW

562
00:34:55,264 --> 00:34:56,705
It will feel empty at first.

563
00:34:58,825 --> 00:34:59,745
Damn.

564
00:34:59,825 --> 00:35:01,185
It really does.

565
00:35:01,265 --> 00:35:02,545
Now I'm sad again.

566
00:35:04,785 --> 00:35:06,305
Then don't fight it.

567
00:35:06,385 --> 00:35:08,665
If you're sad,
be as sad as you need to be.

568
00:36:16,385 --> 00:36:17,625
That's enough.

569
00:36:18,305 --> 00:36:19,745
My hair's a bird's nest now.

570
00:36:20,785 --> 00:36:22,145
A bird's nest?

571
00:36:22,225 --> 00:36:24,185
Come here. I'll fix it.

572
00:36:30,305 --> 00:36:32,425
So, do you feel better?

573
00:36:34,265 --> 00:36:35,665
Yeah, I do.

574
00:36:35,745 --> 00:36:37,305
It feels strangely good.

575
00:36:38,025 --> 00:36:39,705
Mostly strange.

576
00:36:39,785 --> 00:36:41,825
Told you it would work.

577
00:36:42,945 --> 00:36:45,105
Yeah. It really did.

578
00:36:46,985 --> 00:36:47,985
So,

579
00:36:48,865 --> 00:36:50,625
are you going anywhere now?

580
00:36:52,545 --> 00:36:53,505
I'm free.

581
00:36:53,585 --> 00:36:55,185
My client just canceled.

582
00:36:56,705 --> 00:36:57,705
Really?

583
00:37:00,065 --> 00:37:01,105
Then come with me.

584
00:37:01,185 --> 00:37:03,345
Want to see my friends play?

585
00:37:03,945 --> 00:37:04,945
Sure.

586
00:37:12,705 --> 00:37:15,265
Didn't Indy and Tungtae come with you?

587
00:37:15,345 --> 00:37:16,345
Oh,

588
00:37:17,345 --> 00:37:19,185
Tae's doing something with his mom.

589
00:37:19,265 --> 00:37:21,905
As for Indy, he's busy trying to move on.

590
00:37:21,985 --> 00:37:23,225
Move on?

591
00:37:23,905 --> 00:37:25,065
Ask him yourself.

592
00:37:25,145 --> 00:37:26,705
Though I don't know if they'll show up.

593
00:37:30,025 --> 00:37:32,145
Hey, Proud's about to go on.

594
00:37:32,225 --> 00:37:33,705
Ready to cheer?

595
00:37:33,785 --> 00:37:34,865
Are you ready?

596
00:37:34,945 --> 00:37:37,825
No. Putter dragged me here.

597
00:37:37,905 --> 00:37:39,545
I'm actually here to cheer
for someone else.

598
00:37:40,145 --> 00:37:41,785
You two need to make up already.

599
00:37:41,865 --> 00:37:43,905
How long are you going to keep this up?

600
00:37:43,985 --> 00:37:45,465
-Are they fake fighting?
-I don't even know her.

601
00:37:45,545 --> 00:37:46,705
That's what I thought.

602
00:37:47,625 --> 00:37:50,305
When will Lazy Meow Meow
get to perform like everyone else?

603
00:37:51,745 --> 00:37:54,425
When people stop saying I play like crap.

604
00:37:55,305 --> 00:37:57,465
Hey, you're really good,

605
00:37:57,545 --> 00:37:58,505
I'm serious.

606
00:37:58,585 --> 00:37:59,825
Have you watched the video?

607
00:37:59,905 --> 00:38:01,705
-Dare to?
-No, thanks.

608
00:38:01,785 --> 00:38:04,145
I'd die of embarrassment.

609
00:38:04,785 --> 00:38:05,745
I'll take your word for it.

610
00:38:07,145 --> 00:38:09,865
-Hey, hey.
-There she is!

611
00:38:15,425 --> 00:38:16,945
That's my friend!

612
00:38:17,545 --> 00:38:18,705
Proud!

613
00:38:29,105 --> 00:38:33,385
<i>We're sitting and gazing</i>
<i>At the sky together just like always</i>

614
00:38:33,465 --> 00:38:37,505
<i>But the feelings I have inside</i>
<i>Have changed</i>

615
00:38:37,585 --> 00:38:39,225
Why does your camera
always drift toward Proud?

616
00:38:40,345 --> 00:38:41,425
Quit calling me out.

617
00:38:43,985 --> 00:38:48,625
<i>Why does it feel so good</i>
<i>Whenever I'm close to you?</i>

618
00:38:48,705 --> 00:38:53,425
<i>I still don't know</i>
<i>If you feel the same way</i>

619
00:38:53,505 --> 00:38:55,745
Here, let me film it. I'm the taller one.

620
00:38:55,825 --> 00:38:57,385
<i>Like this</i>

621
00:38:57,465 --> 00:39:02,865
<i>The closer I get</i>
<i>The more I start to fall</i>

622
00:39:02,945 --> 00:39:07,865
<i>The closer I am to you</i>
<i>The better it feels every time</i>

623
00:39:07,945 --> 00:39:12,705
<i>Is this what love feels like?</i>

624
00:39:12,785 --> 00:39:15,145
<i>Should I just be a good friend</i>

625
00:39:15,225 --> 00:39:19,025
<i>Or should I speak up</i>
<i>And say I love you?</i>

626
00:39:32,345 --> 00:39:34,145
Hey! Indy!

627
00:39:34,825 --> 00:39:35,665
You came?

628
00:39:35,745 --> 00:39:37,665
-Damn!
-Hey!

629
00:39:37,745 --> 00:39:39,145
You look amazing today.

630
00:39:39,225 --> 00:39:41,185
Looking handsome. What did you do?

631
00:39:41,265 --> 00:39:43,305
Jia deserves the credit.

632
00:39:45,025 --> 00:39:46,465
Today, we also have our friends

633
00:39:46,545 --> 00:39:48,425
from Lazy Meow Meow with us.

634
00:39:53,465 --> 00:39:58,145
A big round of applause
for Indy and LeeIth!

635
00:40:00,825 --> 00:40:03,945
-Damn, it took forever to get here.
-Where's your mom?

636
00:40:04,025 --> 00:40:05,545
-Where did she go?
-Forget about my mom.

637
00:40:05,625 --> 00:40:06,785
-We've been waiting forever.
-I rushed over.

638
00:40:06,865 --> 00:40:07,745
Hey, teacher… I mean,

639
00:40:07,825 --> 00:40:08,785
Jia, you're here too?

640
00:40:08,865 --> 00:40:10,385
Man, I missed you. It's been a while.

641
00:40:10,465 --> 00:40:11,665
-Putter, hey.
-Hey.

642
00:40:11,745 --> 00:40:13,545
Hey, Summer. Hey, Yihwa.

643
00:40:13,625 --> 00:40:14,505
Hey, Min.

644
00:40:14,585 --> 00:40:15,985
Hi.

645
00:40:16,985 --> 00:40:19,105
Let's hear it for Lazy Meow Meow!

646
00:40:23,985 --> 00:40:27,825
<i>I've been in love with you for so long</i>

647
00:40:27,905 --> 00:40:31,425
<i>I want to tell you, I want to tell you</i>
<i>But I never have the guts</i>

648
00:40:31,505 --> 00:40:36,665
<i>I'm glad that today</i>
<i>You'll finally know that</i>

649
00:40:36,745 --> 00:40:39,025
<i>It's just that, it's just that</i>

650
00:40:39,105 --> 00:40:42,905
<i>I don't want to be just friends anymore</i>
<i>Let me be more than that</i>

651
00:40:42,985 --> 00:40:44,825
<i>There's only you, only you</i>

652
00:40:44,905 --> 00:40:46,705
<i>I wish we loved each other</i>

653
00:40:46,785 --> 00:40:52,025
<i>I want you to know that today</i>

654
00:40:52,105 --> 00:40:54,225
<i>I don't want to be</i>
<i>Just your friend anymore</i>

655
00:40:54,305 --> 00:40:56,665
<i>The one standing next to that guy.</i>

656
00:40:57,265 --> 00:40:58,425
The one with the big eyes.

657
00:40:58,505 --> 00:41:01,065
He's so damn cute when he smiles.

658
00:41:01,705 --> 00:41:03,225
Yeah, he's cute.

659
00:41:22,625 --> 00:41:27,185
<i>I really don't know</i>
<i>If you feel the same way</i>

660
00:41:27,265 --> 00:41:30,305
<i>If I say it out loud, will I lose you?</i>

661
00:41:35,225 --> 00:41:36,505
Damn.

662
00:41:37,185 --> 00:41:39,225
Why does his camera keep pointing at me?

663
00:41:42,065 --> 00:41:43,385
I'd better search it.

664
00:41:48,625 --> 00:41:51,545
WHY DOES MY HEART RACE
AROUND MY BEST FRIEND?

665
00:41:55,465 --> 00:41:56,545
Too long.

666
00:42:02,585 --> 00:42:04,145
<i>A racing heart around a friend</i>

667
00:42:04,225 --> 00:42:05,825
<i>can be caused by psychology or hormones.</i>

668
00:42:06,665 --> 00:42:07,905
Hormones?

669
00:42:09,185 --> 00:42:10,705
Psychology?

670
00:42:11,785 --> 00:42:14,025
-And…
<i>-Or feelings beyond friendship.</i>

671
00:42:14,105 --> 00:42:16,385
No way.

672
00:42:16,465 --> 00:42:18,345
We're just friends, aren't we?

673
00:42:26,065 --> 00:42:27,625
Why were you in the bathroom so long?

674
00:42:28,665 --> 00:42:31,065
-What's with you?
-I'm fine.

675
00:42:31,145 --> 00:42:32,305
That's my business, isn't it?

676
00:42:34,705 --> 00:42:36,105
What's with him?

677
00:42:42,545 --> 00:42:43,505
Why didn't he turn off the tap?

678
00:42:59,625 --> 00:43:01,065
Pull it in, Tun.

679
00:43:01,145 --> 00:43:02,625
Nice.

680
00:43:05,665 --> 00:43:06,745
Too weak.

681
00:43:07,705 --> 00:43:09,185
I was flirting with their side.

682
00:43:10,865 --> 00:43:11,985
Then don't flirt too much.

683
00:43:19,865 --> 00:43:21,385
Why?

684
00:43:21,465 --> 00:43:22,705
Afraid you'll fall for me?

685
00:43:29,825 --> 00:43:32,105
No, you'll make us lose.

686
00:43:32,185 --> 00:43:33,705
Then I'll lose all my stars.

687
00:43:40,025 --> 00:43:41,545
You haven't eaten?

688
00:43:42,105 --> 00:43:45,545
Yeah. I was too excited tonight,
so I skipped dinner.

689
00:43:47,625 --> 00:43:48,985
I'll cook for you.

690
00:43:50,505 --> 00:43:51,785
Then we'll be even.

691
00:44:03,825 --> 00:44:05,385
Done!

692
00:44:06,185 --> 00:44:08,185
Presented by the son of an Iron Chef.

693
00:44:09,705 --> 00:44:11,705
Railway fried rice.

694
00:44:13,225 --> 00:44:14,265
It looks pretty good.

695
00:44:16,265 --> 00:44:17,825
How does it taste?

696
00:44:25,785 --> 00:44:26,785
Well?

697
00:44:27,865 --> 00:44:29,305
Be honest with me.

698
00:44:30,585 --> 00:44:32,465
Honestly,

699
00:44:32,545 --> 00:44:34,625
-It's not very good.
-Really?

700
00:44:38,585 --> 00:44:39,585
It's not that good.

701
00:44:39,665 --> 00:44:41,585
Is your mom really a chef?

702
00:44:43,825 --> 00:44:44,985
Let me try it.

703
00:44:50,705 --> 00:44:51,665
Well?

704
00:44:51,745 --> 00:44:53,105
I'm screwed.

705
00:44:54,065 --> 00:44:55,705
I didn't even taste it first.

706
00:44:55,785 --> 00:44:57,825
I was a little too confident.

707
00:44:59,745 --> 00:45:02,305
Honestly, it would probably be fine
with a fried egg.

708
00:45:02,985 --> 00:45:04,705
It's okay. You don't have to eat it.

709
00:45:04,785 --> 00:45:06,225
I'll order you something instead.

710
00:45:06,905 --> 00:45:08,105
It's fine.

711
00:45:21,145 --> 00:45:23,065
Are you eating it just to cheer me up?

712
00:45:26,265 --> 00:45:27,625
It's edible.

713
00:45:28,985 --> 00:45:30,185
But yeah.

714
00:45:32,625 --> 00:45:34,505
You told me to cheer you up, didn't you?

715
00:45:42,625 --> 00:45:43,945
Thanks.

716
00:45:44,025 --> 00:45:46,305
I'll do better next time.

717
00:45:48,505 --> 00:45:50,705
I'm going to bed.

718
00:45:52,505 --> 00:45:53,625
Hey, not yet.

719
00:45:53,705 --> 00:45:56,025
You'll get acid reflux if you
sleep right after eating.

720
00:45:56,745 --> 00:45:58,585
Sir, I know that.

721
00:45:58,665 --> 00:46:00,265
I'll sit around for a while first.

722
00:46:00,345 --> 00:46:01,545
Yeah. Thank you.

723
00:46:01,625 --> 00:46:02,785
Bye.

724
00:46:29,865 --> 00:46:31,105
You've got a lot of stuff.

725
00:46:32,585 --> 00:46:33,825
Yeah.

726
00:46:33,905 --> 00:46:35,825
They told us to bring the props.

727
00:46:35,905 --> 00:46:38,465
Here, let me carry this.

728
00:46:38,545 --> 00:46:39,745
I want to look cool.

729
00:46:40,825 --> 00:46:42,625
Not sure about that.

730
00:46:43,545 --> 00:46:44,905
You talk too much.

731
00:46:44,985 --> 00:46:46,505
Not even a thank you?

732
00:46:47,385 --> 00:46:49,865
Alright, thanks.

733
00:47:16,425 --> 00:47:17,425
Damn!

734
00:47:19,305 --> 00:47:20,305
Get out!

735
00:47:21,025 --> 00:47:21,865
You're so slow.

736
00:47:21,945 --> 00:47:23,705
You'll get what's coming.

737
00:47:37,145 --> 00:47:39,225
Hey, where are you rushing off to?

738
00:47:39,305 --> 00:47:40,385
The crosswalk's right here.

739
00:47:40,465 --> 00:47:41,785
PLEASE WAIT FOR WALK SIGNAL

740
00:47:41,865 --> 00:47:44,345
Crossing here is basically the same.

741
00:47:44,425 --> 00:47:47,185
-It's faster, too.
-But the crosswalk's safer.

742
00:47:47,785 --> 00:47:48,785
Let's go.

743
00:47:52,345 --> 00:47:53,385
PLEASE WAIT FOR WALK SIGNAL

744
00:48:07,065 --> 00:48:08,705
Were you worried about me?

745
00:48:10,585 --> 00:48:11,665
Yeah.

746
00:48:13,745 --> 00:48:15,025
If you'd gotten hit,

747
00:48:15,105 --> 00:48:16,745
I'd have to take responsibility again.

748
00:48:16,825 --> 00:48:18,465
Your mom would kill me.

749
00:48:19,145 --> 00:48:21,865
Besides, if you crossed there,

750
00:48:22,465 --> 00:48:23,625
you would hold up traffic.

751
00:48:23,705 --> 00:48:25,745
You'd be the one causing traffic in Siam.

752
00:48:27,665 --> 00:48:29,665
Alright, Dad.

753
00:48:29,745 --> 00:48:31,545
I gave in the moment you said, "Yeah."

754
00:48:33,585 --> 00:48:34,545
Oh, right.

755
00:48:34,625 --> 00:48:36,385
Can you go somewhere with me after school?

756
00:48:38,465 --> 00:48:40,425
Sure. Let's go.

757
00:48:50,905 --> 00:48:52,905
Damn. It's beautiful.

758
00:48:52,985 --> 00:48:55,105
It does look nice.

759
00:49:00,425 --> 00:49:02,545
Hold on. That's 10,000 baht.

760
00:49:02,625 --> 00:49:04,425
If you spend that much,

761
00:49:04,505 --> 00:49:05,425
I'm telling your mom.

762
00:49:06,105 --> 00:49:09,065
I'm not scared. It's my savings.

763
00:49:09,145 --> 00:49:10,145
I can buy whatever I want.

764
00:49:13,545 --> 00:49:16,105
I know the more expensive the headphones,

765
00:49:16,185 --> 00:49:18,225
the better they are,
but is it really necessary?

766
00:49:18,305 --> 00:49:19,785
Of course it is.

767
00:49:19,865 --> 00:49:22,785
This way,
I can practice without disturbing you.

768
00:49:22,865 --> 00:49:24,065
Look at Tae.

769
00:49:24,145 --> 00:49:27,025
He stepped on mine and broke it.

770
00:49:36,705 --> 00:49:40,145
So, you haven't practiced music
at all these past two weeks?

771
00:49:41,505 --> 00:49:43,585
I didn't want to bother you
since you were studying for finals.

772
00:49:44,265 --> 00:49:45,265
And playing games too.

773
00:50:07,825 --> 00:50:11,025
Damn, this is so good. Give it a listen.

774
00:50:29,545 --> 00:50:30,385
It's pretty good.

775
00:50:32,665 --> 00:50:34,105
Told you.

776
00:50:56,545 --> 00:50:58,825
<i>If the rule is not to fall</i>
<i>for someone close to you,</i>

777
00:50:58,905 --> 00:51:00,105
<i>then does that mean…?</i>

778
00:51:00,945 --> 00:51:02,505
<i>I wish I could take a tour of your mind.</i>

779
00:51:02,585 --> 00:51:03,945
<i>To see what you're thinking.</i>

780
00:51:07,945 --> 00:51:09,225
<i>When I said I was laughing,</i>

781
00:51:09,305 --> 00:51:11,985
<i>actually, I think I was just embarrassed.</i>

782
00:51:12,065 --> 00:51:13,585
I DON'T THINK #TERLEEITH ARE JUST FRIENDS.

783
00:51:13,665 --> 00:51:14,985
DOES PUTTER SMILE LIKE THAT TO EVERYONE
OR JUST LEEITH?

784
00:51:15,065 --> 00:51:16,185
GUYS, I WANT TO ANNOUNCE THAT PUTTER
IS LEEITH'S BOYFRIEND. END OF DISCUSSION.

785
00:51:16,265 --> 00:51:17,265
LEEITH AND PUTTER ARE ROOMMATES
BUT KEPT IT FROM THEIR CLUB FRIENDS.

786
00:51:17,345 --> 00:51:18,505
THEY'RE JUST SITTING BESIDE EACH OTHER
AND HERE I AM WRITING THEIR WEDDING SCENE.

787
00:51:18,585 --> 00:51:19,705
GET #TERLEEITH OUT OF MY HEAD.
I HAVE AN EXAM COMING UP.

788
00:51:19,785 --> 00:51:21,065
WHEN THEY MAKE IT OFFICIAL, I'LL SET OFF
FIREWORKS NEAR THE PRINCIPAL'S OFFICE.

789
00:51:21,145 --> 00:51:22,465
YOU CAN SUE ME FOR BEING DELULU,
BUT I SAW THEM BEING SO ROMANTIC TODAY.

790
00:51:26,385 --> 00:51:28,025
<i>If you have a crush on your friend,</i>

791
00:51:28,105 --> 00:51:29,985
<i>should you tell them or not?</i>

792
00:51:49,305 --> 00:51:50,305
NOWADAYS, IF YOU LIKE SOMEONE,
JUST TELL THEM.

793
00:51:50,385 --> 00:51:51,505
IF IT DOESN'T WORK OUT,
YOU'LL MOVE ON SOON ENOUGH.

794
00:51:51,585 --> 00:51:52,545
THAT'S HOW WE STARTED.
IF I HADN'T CONFESSED

795
00:51:52,625 --> 00:51:53,545
THAT DAY, WE WOULDN'T BE WHERE WE ARE NOW.

796
00:51:53,625 --> 00:51:54,625
I HOPE THE ANSWER
IS WHAT YOU'RE WISHING FOR.

797
00:51:54,705 --> 00:51:55,705
YOU'LL NEVER KNOW UNLESS YOU TRY.

798
00:51:55,785 --> 00:51:56,785
JUST HAVING THE COURAGE TO EXPRESS

799
00:51:56,865 --> 00:51:57,905
YOUR FEELINGS IS ALREADY
AMAZING. YOU GOT THIS!

800
00:51:57,985 --> 00:51:58,905
HOPE "FRIEND" TURNS INTO "BOYFRIEND."

801
00:51:58,985 --> 00:52:03,985
GO FOR IT. I'M ROOTING FOR YOU.
I'LL BE WAITING FOR AN UPDATE.

802
00:52:24,265 --> 00:52:25,505
<i>Are you at Siam?</i>

803
00:52:31,625 --> 00:52:33,305
I didn't think you'd message me.

804
00:52:33,385 --> 00:52:35,225
I thought you were on Summer's side.

805
00:52:36,025 --> 00:52:37,585
I'm staying neutral.

806
00:52:37,665 --> 00:52:40,225
So, are you two still mad at each other?

807
00:52:41,025 --> 00:52:43,065
I'm over it, but she isn't.

808
00:52:43,145 --> 00:52:44,905
I'm figuring out how to make it up to her.

809
00:52:44,985 --> 00:52:47,065
Alright, I'll help.

810
00:52:47,145 --> 00:52:48,305
Let's deal with your problem first.

811
00:52:48,385 --> 00:52:50,225
So, what do you want to ask your big sis?

812
00:52:53,585 --> 00:52:54,505
It's about love, isn't it?

813
00:52:56,465 --> 00:52:57,585
Damn,

814
00:52:57,665 --> 00:52:59,185
-How did you know?
-I'm good, right?

815
00:52:59,865 --> 00:53:00,865
You're the best, Sis.

816
00:53:00,945 --> 00:53:02,185
So, what's going on?

817
00:53:08,265 --> 00:53:10,185
What made you…

818
00:53:10,945 --> 00:53:12,185
confess to Summer?

819
00:53:14,785 --> 00:53:16,705
It sounds cliché, but…

820
00:53:16,785 --> 00:53:18,665
I was afraid I'd regret not telling her.

821
00:53:34,745 --> 00:53:36,105
Want me to help?

822
00:53:44,985 --> 00:53:47,665
<i>Back in Grade 8, Summer said</i>
<i>she was transferring schools.</i>

823
00:53:49,585 --> 00:53:52,745
<i>Every day, I felt more and more uneasy.</i>

824
00:53:53,625 --> 00:53:56,305
<i>I was afraid she'd never be</i>
<i>the same if I told her.</i>

825
00:54:00,705 --> 00:54:03,585
<i>But I was even more afraid</i>
<i>I'd regret it forever if I didn't.</i>

826
00:54:10,545 --> 00:54:11,865
<i>So I realized…</i>

827
00:54:12,465 --> 00:54:14,145
<i>I was more afraid of regretting it.</i>

828
00:54:15,545 --> 00:54:16,825
Look over there.

829
00:54:17,545 --> 00:54:18,425
Look.

830
00:54:25,385 --> 00:54:26,945
There's something I want to tell you.

831
00:54:33,825 --> 00:54:35,425
Let's be together, Summer.

832
00:54:39,705 --> 00:54:40,985
So, is that a yes?

833
00:54:45,585 --> 00:54:48,785
<i>It turned out to be</i>
<i>the best decision of my life.</i>

834
00:54:55,025 --> 00:54:56,665
Why are you two so romantic?

835
00:54:57,425 --> 00:54:59,865
That's how Wattanakanlaya's top
couple does it.

836
00:55:15,345 --> 00:55:16,305
I think I have my answer now.

837
00:55:16,905 --> 00:55:18,905
Then I'll be waiting to see what happens.

838
00:55:21,345 --> 00:55:22,905
Thank you so much, Sis.

839
00:55:22,985 --> 00:55:24,265
Thank you so much.

840
00:55:25,305 --> 00:55:26,785
Alright, I'm off.

841
00:55:47,905 --> 00:55:50,505
Hey, I have something to tell you.

842
00:57:09,865 --> 00:57:10,905
Hey.

843
00:57:11,825 --> 00:57:12,985
Pay attention in class.

844
00:57:34,905 --> 00:57:37,705
<i>Hey, I have something to tell you.</i>

845
00:57:43,385 --> 00:57:44,705
I'm sorry.

846
00:57:45,385 --> 00:57:47,105
For not telling you in person.

847
00:57:50,105 --> 00:57:51,625
I wasn't brave enough,

848
00:57:54,265 --> 00:57:55,985
because I was afraid of your reaction.

849
00:57:57,265 --> 00:58:00,385
<i>I wanted to thank you</i>

850
00:58:02,545 --> 00:58:05,345
<i>for always looking after me,</i>
<i>caring about me,</i>

851
00:58:06,585 --> 00:58:10,105
<i>and making me feel so comfortable</i>
<i>being myself.</i>

852
00:58:13,625 --> 00:58:15,545
After saying all of that,

853
00:58:15,625 --> 00:58:16,905
what I really want to tell you is…

854
00:58:33,145 --> 00:58:34,825
I like you.

855
00:58:34,905 --> 00:58:37,665
Break that rule and be my boyfriend.

856
00:58:39,985 --> 00:58:42,825
<i>Shit. What the hell am I saying?</i>

857
01:00:08,745 --> 01:00:09,745
Damn it.

858
01:00:30,225 --> 01:00:31,225
Why didn't you answer my calls?

859
01:00:35,345 --> 01:00:37,425
My phone died, and I forgot my charger.

860
01:00:41,785 --> 01:00:42,905
Well…

861
01:00:46,145 --> 01:00:47,105
I listened to it.

862
01:00:48,905 --> 01:00:52,185
You did? So, what do you think?

863
01:00:55,905 --> 01:00:57,505
After I heard it,

864
01:00:59,385 --> 01:01:01,785
I finally realized who

865
01:01:01,865 --> 01:01:05,185
the reading meant when it said
someone would confess to you.

866
01:01:07,905 --> 01:01:09,105
Who?

867
01:01:13,265 --> 01:01:14,545
Me.

868
01:01:15,345 --> 01:01:18,625
And now I'm sure that reading was right.

869
01:01:19,865 --> 01:01:23,025
I've… been fighting the voice
in my head for so long.

870
01:01:25,865 --> 01:01:27,025
But today…

871
01:01:28,465 --> 01:01:30,305
I think I'm done fighting it.

872
01:01:34,305 --> 01:01:36,025
What did that voice say?

873
01:01:41,145 --> 01:01:42,425
Well…

874
01:01:43,705 --> 01:01:45,425
Will you give me a chance?

875
01:01:49,545 --> 01:01:50,625
As your boyfriend.

876
01:01:57,505 --> 01:01:59,425
I'm ready to break the rule.

877
01:02:00,585 --> 01:02:01,425
What about you?

878
01:02:12,465 --> 01:02:13,785
If I wasn't ready to break the rule,

879
01:02:14,465 --> 01:02:16,705
why would I record
that confession on your laptop?

880
01:02:18,545 --> 01:02:20,945
So, you…

881
01:02:21,025 --> 01:02:22,945
I'm saying yes.

882
01:02:23,025 --> 01:02:24,665
Don't be so clueless now.

883
01:02:32,865 --> 01:02:33,865
Here.

884
01:02:34,625 --> 01:02:36,825
A gift for our first day together.

885
01:02:37,345 --> 01:02:39,105
It was buy one, get one free.

886
01:02:50,145 --> 01:02:51,345
Damn, what did I just say?

887
01:02:55,825 --> 01:02:56,745
Hey,

888
01:02:57,625 --> 01:02:59,145
why are you hiding from me?

889
01:02:59,665 --> 01:03:01,505
I want to see you blush.

890
01:03:02,305 --> 01:03:03,585
Alright, alright. Let's go.

891
01:03:03,665 --> 01:03:05,425
Let's head back to our room.

892
01:03:06,345 --> 01:03:07,425
Our room?

893
01:03:07,505 --> 01:03:08,945
Don't get all cheesy.

894
01:03:16,945 --> 01:03:18,145
What are you doing?

895
01:03:22,705 --> 01:03:24,785
"Our first-day-together gift."

896
01:03:24,865 --> 01:03:25,785
Not cheesy at all, huh?

897
01:03:26,825 --> 01:03:28,785
That's enough.
I'm not listening. Let's go.

898
01:03:28,865 --> 01:03:30,425
Let's head back.

899
01:03:30,505 --> 01:03:32,105
Yeah, let's go.

900
01:03:32,185 --> 01:03:34,345
-Hey, wait for me!
-Come on, let's go.

901
01:04:09,665 --> 01:04:11,105
Make it look natural.

902
01:04:11,185 --> 01:04:12,385
<i>Yeah, yeah.</i>

903
01:04:14,505 --> 01:04:16,105
Putter.

904
01:04:17,105 --> 01:04:18,305
<i>Werewolf, close your eyes.</i>

905
01:04:19,705 --> 01:04:20,985
You like this one.

906
01:04:21,065 --> 01:04:23,345
<i>Is there anything you're hiding from me?</i>

907
01:04:23,425 --> 01:04:25,305
-<i>No.</i>
-You've been lonely lately.

908
01:04:25,385 --> 01:04:26,945
Feeling neglected and suspicious.

909
01:04:27,545 --> 01:04:29,265
<i>If you don't want me</i>
<i>as your friend anymore,</i>

910
01:04:29,345 --> 01:04:31,265
<i>just say it, damn it.</i>

911
01:04:32,225 --> 01:04:33,105
<i>Is that a new perfume?</i>

912
01:04:33,185 --> 01:04:34,345
That's the same scent Indy wears.

913
01:04:34,425 --> 01:04:36,225
<i>LeeIth, have you seen this?</i>

914
01:04:36,305 --> 01:04:38,105
<i>The Brain Drain Gang found</i>
<i>Putter's secret account.</i>

